      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T06:34:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that makes sense. \n\nthe actual change is a bit tricky, as the number of host entries of leaf4 could be different from the default one. So when enforcing a host leaf4 entry, the index may not exist in default which is different from other enforced leaves. and even if it exists, we will fill it with hard-coded 64 bytes instead of using the default value. Then when appending a default leaf4 entry, it should be done only when there is no any leaf4 entry in the host buffer. Otherwise appending should be skipped as the host decides the hierarchy (if smaller than the native).\n\nI\u0027ll see how to make it simple/clean.",
